       "    </tr>\n",
       "    <tr>\n",
       "      <th>2017-05-02 19:08:37</th>\n",
       "      <td>5.922730</td>\n",
       "      <td>10.128382</td>\n",
       "    </tr>\n",
       "    <tr>\n",
       "      <th>2017-05-02 20:08:37</th>\n",
       "      <td>5.999581</td>\n",
       "      <td>10.290300</td>\n",
       "    </tr>\n",
       "    <tr>\n",
       "      <th>2017-05-02 21:08:37</th>\n",
       "      <td>6.031067</td>\n",
       "      <td>8.910037</td>\n",
       "    </tr>\n",
       "  </tbody>\n",
       "</table>\n",
       "</div>"
      ],
      "text/plain": [
       "                     Speed (kRPM)  Power (kW)\n",
       "Time                                         \n",
       "2017-05-02 17:08:37      6.066579   10.308257\n",
       "2017-05-02 18:08:37      6.035764    9.186763\n",
       "2017-05-02 19:08:37      5.922730   10.128382\n",
       "2017-05-02 20:08:37      5.999581   10.290300\n",
       "2017-05-02 21:08:37      6.031067    8.910037"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 29,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "df = pd.read_csv('./data/generator.csv', index_col=\"Time\", parse_dates=True)\n",
    "df = validate_series(df)\n",
    "df.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 30,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def myDetectionFunc(df):\n",
    "    return (df[\"Speed (kRPM)\"] * 1.2 > df[\"Power (kW)\"])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 31,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "\n",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1152x288 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from adtk.detector import CustomizedDetectorHD\n",
    "customized_detector = CustomizedDetectorHD(detect_func=myDetectionFunc)\n",
    "anomalies = customized_detector.detect(df)\n",
    "plot(df, anomaly=anomalies, ts_linewidth=1, ts_markersize=3, anomaly_color='red', anomaly_alpha=0.3, curve_group='all');"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Transformer"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### RollingAggregate"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "`RollingAggregate` rolls a sliding window along a time series and aggregates using a selected operation. Common examples including moving average, rolling standard deviation, etc.\n",
    "\n",
    "In the following example, we track the rolling count of valid values along a time series, which may help raise alarm when missing values occur frequently."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 32,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "\n",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1152x288 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "s = pd.read_csv('./data/pressure.csv', index_col=\"Time\", parse_dates=True, squeeze=True)\n",
    "s = validate_series(s)\n",
    "plot(s, ts_linewidth=1, ts_markersize=4);"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 33,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "\n",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1152x288 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from adtk.transformer import RollingAggregate\n",
    "s_transformed = RollingAggregate(agg='count', window=5).transform(s)\n",
    "plot(s_transformed.rename(\"Rolling count of valid values\"), ts_linewidth=1, ts_markersize=4);"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### DoubleRollingAggregate"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "`DoubleRollingAggregate` rolls two sliding windows side-by-side along a time series, aggregates using a selected operation, and tracks difference of the aggregated metrics between the two windows. This may help tracking changes of statistical behavior in a time series.\n",
    "\n",
    "In the following example, we track the change of statistical distribution of series values."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 34,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "\n",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1152x576 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "s = pd.read_csv('./data/seismic.csv', index_col=\"Time\", parse_dates=True, squeeze=True)\n",
    "s = validate_series(s)\n",
    "\n",
    "from adtk.transformer import DoubleRollingAggregate\n",
    "s_transformed = DoubleRollingAggregate(\n",
    "    agg=\"quantile\", \n",
    "    agg_params={\"q\": [0.1, 0.5, 0.9]}, \n",
    "    window=50,\n",
    "    diff=\"l2\").transform(s).rename(\"Diff rolling quantiles (mm)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plot(pd.concat([s, s_transformed], axis=1));"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "In the following example, we track the shift of value level."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 35,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "s = pd.read_csv('./data/cpu.csv', index_col=\"Time\", parse_dates=True, squeeze=True)\n",
    "s = validate_series(s)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 36,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "\n",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1152x576 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from adtk.transformer import DoubleRollingAggregate\n",
    "s_transformed = DoubleRollingAggregate(\n",
    "    agg=\"median\", \n",
    "    window=5,\n",
    "    diff=\"diff\").transform(s).rename(\"Diff rolling median (mm)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plot(pd.concat([s, s_transformed], axis=1));"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "In the following example, we track the anomalous changes of price by adjusting the window parameter."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 37,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "s = pd.read_csv('./data/price_short.csv', index_col=\"Time\", parse_dates=True, squeeze=True)\n",
    "s = validate_series(s)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 38,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "\n",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1152x576 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from adtk.transformer import DoubleRollingAggregate\n",
    "s_transformed = DoubleRollingAggregate(\n",
    "    agg=\"mean\", \n",
    "    window=(3,1), #The tuple specifies the left window to be 3, and right window to be 1\n",
    "    diff=\"l1\").transform(s).rename(\"Diff rolling mean with different window size\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plot(pd.concat([s, s_transformed], axis=1), ts_linewidth=1, ts_markersize=3);"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### ClassicSeasonalDecomposition"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "`ClassicSeasonalDecomposition` decomposes a series into trend part (optional), seasonal part and residual part. The residual part may help identifying anomalous deviation from seasonal pattern.\n",
    "\n",
    "In the following example, we calculate the deviation from usual traffic pattern along the series, which may help identify unusual traffic."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 39,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "s = pd.read_csv('./data/seasonal.csv', index_col=\"Time\", parse_dates=True, squeeze=True)\n",
    "s = validate_series(s)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 40,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "\n",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1152x576 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from adtk.transformer import ClassicSeasonalDecomposition\n",
    "s_transformed = ClassicSeasonalDecomposition().fit_transform(s).rename(\"Seasonal decomposition residual\")\n",
    "plot(pd.concat([s, s_transformed], axis=1), ts_markersize=1);"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "`ClassicSeasonalDecomposition` without extracting trend could not handle cases where long-term trend is mixed with seasonal pattern as well as noise. In those cases, option `trend` should be turned on.\n",
    "\n",
    "In the following example, `ClassicSeasonalDecomposition` fails to decompose residual series and long-term trend from a synthetic series without `trend` option turned on."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 41,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "s = pd.read_csv('./data/seasonal+trend.csv', index_col=\"Time\", parse_dates=True, squeeze=True)\n",
    "s = validate_series(s)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 42,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "\n",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1152x576 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "s_transformed = ClassicSeasonalDecomposition(freq=7).fit_transform(s).rename(\"Seasonal decomposition residual and trend\")\n",
    "plot(pd.concat([s, s_transformed], axis=1), ts_linewidth=1, ts_markersize=4);"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We turn on the `trend` option of the model and re-apply to the same example as above, where residual is separated from trend."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 43,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "\n",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1152x576 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "s_transformed = ClassicSeasonalDecomposition(freq=7, trend=True).fit_transform(s).rename(\"Seasonal decomposition residual\")\n",
    "plot(pd.concat([s, s_transformed], axis=1), ts_linewidth=1, ts_markersize=4);"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Retrospect"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "`Retrospect` returns data frame with retrospective values, i.e. a row at time t includes value at (t-k)'s where k's are specified by user. This transformer may be useful for cases where lagging effect should be taken into account. \n",
    "\n",
    "In the following example, we create a retrospective data frame for a synthetic series."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 44,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "s = pd.read_csv('./data/sin.csv', index_col=\"Time\", parse_dates=True, squeeze=True)\n",
    "s = validate_series(s)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 45,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "\n",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1152x288 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from adtk.transformer import Retrospect\n",
    "df = Retrospect(n_steps=4, step_size=20, till=50).transform(s)\n",
    "plot(pd.concat([s, df], axis=1), curve_group=\"all\");"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### RegressionResidual"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "`RegressionResidual` performs regression to a multivariate series and returns regressive residual. This may help identifying anomalous violation of usual relationship between series.\n",
    "\n",
    "In the following example, we track deviation of series from usual correlation between generator speed and power."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 46,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df = pd.read_csv('./data/generator.csv', index_col=\"Time\", parse_dates=True)\n",
    "df = validate_series(df)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 47,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "\n",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1152x576 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from adtk.transformer import RegressionResidual\n",
    "s = RegressionResidual(regressor=LinearRegression(), target=\"Speed (kRPM)\").fit_transform(df).rename(\"Regression residual (kRPM)\")\n",
    "plot(pd.concat([df, s], axis=1), ts_linewidth=1, ts_markersize=3, curve_group=[(\"Speed (kRPM)\", \"Power (kW)\"), \"Regression residual (kRPM)\"]);"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### PcaProjection"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "`PcaProjection` transforms a multivariate series into representation with first k principal components.\n",
    "\n",
    "In the following example, we transform the 2-dimensional series used in the previous example into 1-dimension by only keeping its first principal coefficient."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 48,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "\n",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1152x576 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from adtk.transformer import PcaProjection\n",
    "s = PcaProjection(k=1).fit_transform(df)\n",
    "plot(pd.concat([df, s], axis=1), ts_linewidth=1, ts_markersize=3, curve_group=[(\"Speed (kRPM)\", \"Power (kW)\"), \"pc0\"]);"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### PcaReconstruction"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "`PcaReconstruction` projects a multivariate series onto the hyperplane spanned by its first k principal components.\n",
    "\n",
    "In the following example, we project the 2-dimensional series used in previous example onto the line of its first principal component."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 49,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "\n",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1152x576 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from adtk.transformer import PcaReconstruction\n",
    "df_transformed = PcaReconstruction(k=1).fit_transform(df).rename(columns={\"Speed (kRPM)\": \"Speed reconstruction (kRPM)\", \"Power (kW)\": \"Power reconstruction (kW)\"})\n",
    "plot(pd.concat([df, df_transformed], axis=1), ts_linewidth=1, ts_markersize=3, curve_group=[(\"Speed (kRPM)\", \"Power (kW)\"), (\"Speed reconstruction (kRPM)\", \"Power reconstruction (kW)\")]);"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### PcaReconstructionError"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "`PcaReconstructionError` projects a multivariate series onto the hyperplane spanned by its first k principal components and returns the error that indicates the distance between the data point and the lower-rank subspace of the first k principal components.\n",
    "\n",
    "In the following example, we project the 2-dimensional series used in previous example onto the line of its first principal component."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 50,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "\n",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1152x576 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from adtk.transformer import PcaReconstructionError\n",
    "s = PcaReconstructionError(k=1).fit_transform(df).rename(\"PCA Reconstruction Error\")\n",
    "plot(pd.concat([df, s], axis=1), ts_linewidth=1, ts_markersize=3, curve_group=[(\"Speed (kRPM)\", \"Power (kW)\"), \"PCA Reconstruction Error\"]);"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### CustomizedTransformer"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Like a customized detector, a user may convert a function to a customized transformer with `CustomizedTransformer1D` or `CustomizedTransformerHD`, so that it can be used by a `Pipe` object.\n",
    "\n",
    "In the following example, we obtained a calculated series of generated power (in kW) divided by generator speed (in kRPM)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 51,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df = pd.read_csv('./data/generator.csv', index_col=\"Time\", parse_dates=True)\n",
    "df = validate_series(df)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 52,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def myTransformationFunc(df):\n",
    "    return (df[\"Power (kW)\"] / df[\"Speed (kRPM)\"]).rename(\"Power/Speed (kW/kRPM)\")"
   ]
  },
